eds with 0 errors. I didn't load it into Grasshopper, so it's untested there.\n\nIt follows the existing `AddComponent` pattern, in category \"Bench\", subcategory \"Math\". Its five inputs are Value, Source Min, Source Max, Target Min and Target Max, and its output is Result. Source Min and Target Min default to 0, and Source Max and Target Max default to 1.\n\nThe result is `t0 + (value - s0) / (s1 - s0) * (t1 - t0)`. It doesn't clamp, so values outside the source range land outside the target range.\n\nI chose one behavior for you: if Source Min equals Source Max, the component shows an error message and outputs nothing instead of dividing by zero.\n\nThe build's two warnings were nuget version-resolution notices for the Grasshopper package, which resolved to 8.0.23304.9001.","ttft_ms":2689,"type":"result","duration_ms":32243,"uuid":"60677603-52c2-42bc-84a5-6d4326203e2f","ttft_stream_ms":2149,"time_to_request_ms":758,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":53,"system_prompt":351,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":27,"input_attachments":138,"input_hooks":39,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":66,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":27,"autocompact":3,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":24},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":370,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":280,"time_to_request_major_faults":4361,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"queued_commands","slowest_producer_ms":83,"cpu_ms":63,"major_faults":701},"first_content_frame_ms":2150,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
